index 3b92038..f79fc49 100644
--- a/docs/phase-1-plan.md
+++ b/docs/phase-1-plan.md
@@ -246,6 +246,8 @@ Guardrail engine, order proposals (tables only), approval UI, submission, bracke
 
 **From the claude-fable phase review (narrowed rerun after two timeouts), fixed:** a snapshot uses only a post-close balance (the intraday fallback would have stamped an 11:00 equity as a close on catch-up and moved the high-water mark); the end-of-day sections say unknown, not none, while the activities feed is stale, and the equity line says stale; catch-up runs activities inline before enqueuing positions so a positions sync landing first cannot plug every trade bought during the pause; the plug price is in the plug's pre-split units; `get_account_health` reports a feed failure by the dashboard's rule (unresolved only); the dashboard's day change is unknown when a flow is unpriced; stop assignment runs only on a complete orders run (a truncated page or an unmapped or unresolved order skips it; a stop Schwab no longer returns does not).
 
+**Delisted holdings (added after the first deploy, 2026-09-01; a §5.2 column the user approved):** `instruments.delisted_at`, set and cleared from the system page (`InstrumentsController#update`, audited as `instrument_delisted` / `instrument_relisted`) and cleared by the positions sync when Schwab prices the holding again (audited as the system). A delisted holding still syncs and stays in the journal; its protection state is `delisted`, which leaves the unprotected count and every risk sum, sorts last on the dashboard, shows as one line in the excluded summary, and is named in the scheduled prompt as never to quote or count.
+
 **Deferred from the phase-level review (do before Phase 2, each gets more expensive weekly):** rename `Dashboard` to `Desk` (five consumers, one of them a screen) and `Agent::Run` to `Agent::Conversation`; fold `SystemStatus` onto the desk read model (halted_by, pause-since, last-sync-per-feed, and the token line are each written twice); one timestamp formatter per audience (the two locale formats for humans, `Agent.serialize` for machines; delete `Brief#stamp` and `Agent::Context#stamp`) and one cost label; move `Playwright::Scenario` to `lib/`; route `Agent::Context`'s setup stats through the registry or a shared method; add `audited` metadata to `Agent::Tool` for write tools; decide the activities policy when Schwab rejects one assumed type every run (today the run fails and re-backfills the window); `risk_rules` global uniqueness needs `NULLS NOT DISTINCT`; one trading account per desk (a validation collides with the factories; a partial unique index when Phase 2 needs it); `Instrument.lookup_cusip` can hit a token refresh inside the journal transaction (narrow); `Sync::CatchUpJob#perform` and the Playwright scenario loader have no Ruby-level specs; `Setup#avg_r` and `#expectancy` carry one number; the `market_hours` feed value is never written.
 
 ## 12. Schwab assumptions to verify on approval
