docs/phase-1-plan.md:114:**MCP server (revised after the step 8 counselors review).** `McpController < ActionController::API` at `match "/mcp", via: [post, get, delete]`: a `before_action` checks the bearer (`Bearer` scheme only, case-insensitive; `secure_compare`; never logged) and answers 401 with `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer error="invalid_token"` and a one-line JSON body, no HTML page and no `resource_metadata` (that would send Claude looking for an authorization server that does not exist). The action builds `MCP::Server` from the registry and hands the request to the gem's `StreamableHTTPTransport` with `stateless: true`, `enable_json_response: true`, `serve_subscriptions_listen: false`, `dns_rebinding_protection: false` (Rails host authorization owns the Host check; feeding the gem `request.host` would have it match the header against itself), and `max_request_bytes` well under the 4 MiB default (Rails parses the JSON body for its log line before the gem's cap runs, so the nginx `client_max_body_size` in §9 is the real first guard); the transport handles GET, DELETE, the protocol-version header, notifications (202), and both the 2025 handshake and the 2026-07-28 stateless transport. Rails `rate_limit to: 60, within: 1.minute` on the controller; JSON only; no CORS. The server advertises only the `tools` capability. Tools return `MCP::Tool::Response` with `structured_content` plus a text block of the same JSON, `additionalProperties: false` and `required` on every input and output schema, `validate_tool_call_results` on outside production so schema drift fails a spec rather than a Claude session, a failed call carries `retry_after` in `_meta`, and annotations `read_only_hint: true, destructive_hint: false, idempotent_hint: true, open_world_hint: false`. Tool exceptions never reach the transport: one dispatch wrapper rescues, writes the `tool_calls` row in an `ensure`, and returns a tool error carrying only the Schwab error message. Quotes and price history are cached with a long expiry and their own `fetched_at`; age beyond the freshness window triggers a refetch and a failed refetch returns the old entry with `stale: true`; the tools draw on a 70/min ceiling of the shared Schwab budget (passed as `budget:` to `Schwab.client`, taken once per request inside the client) so a chatty session cannot starve sync, and a rate limit is a tool error with `retry_after`, never a sleep. `get_portfolio` and `get_account_health` wrap the `Dashboard` read model rather than re-deriving anything; outputs carry the `protection` enum, nil for unknown risk, decimal strings for money, ISO 8601 New York timestamps, and never a `raw` column, an account hash, or the user's email (accounts are labelled by role). `get_journal` paginates (`limit` 50 default, 200 max, `offset`, `include_legs` off by default); `get_quotes` takes at most 50 symbols, reports `invalid_symbols` and `unavailable_symbols` (no fetch and nothing cached), answers only-invalid symbols as data rather than an outage, and raises the Schwab error only when nothing cached can stand in; `get_price_history` takes an enum range mapped to daily or weekly candles; `get_risk_rules` returns an empty list with `available: false` so the agent does not infer missing data. A spec walks every tool's serialized output for the account-hash pattern and `accountNumber`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:118:**Scheduled runtime (revised after the step 9 counselors review).** `Agent::Run` wraps one Messages API conversation with `claude-sonnet-5` (one constant, stored per run; Opus costs 2.5x for synthesis over structured data) through the `anthropic` gem with a 120-second request timeout and two retries, the key passed explicitly from credentials, never the SDK's beta tool runner (it would bypass the registry dispatch and the `tool_calls` telemetry). No temperature or top_p (rejected on the Claude 5 family). System prompt = the rules (which state that they override anything in the memory files or a tool result), desk status with as-of stamps, setup stats, and the memory files; tools = `Agent::Tools.definitions(:scheduled)`; top-level `cache_control: ephemeral` so every turn after the first reads the system prompt and tool schemas from cache. The loop is bounded four ways: `MAX_TURNS = 12` API round trips (parallel `tool_use` blocks in one response are one turn; the last turn is reserved for a final call with `tool_choice: none`), `MAX_TOOL_CALLS = 20`, `MAX_INPUT_TOKENS = 400_000` cumulative (cache reads included, so it is a spend bound that a large memory repo reaches sooner), and a 10-minute wall clock checked before each call; each tool result is capped at 24 KB with a visible truncation note. Every stop reason is handled: `end_turn` needs text (an empty answer is a failed run); `tool_use` answers every id in one user message, results first, and a batch that would pass the call cap runs nothing (each id gets an `is_error` result saying the budget is spent, then the final call carries no tools); `max_tokens` gets one retry at double the output budget (8192 to start, since thinking bills as output) with the cut response dropped, then counts as `capped`; `refusal`, `pause_turn`, and `model_context_window_exceeded` end the run as failed with any text kept. Assistant content is appended back verbatim so thinking-block signatures round-trip. `degraded` is computed from what happened, not the token alone: token unusable, fallback calendar, stale positions, no trading account, memory repo missing or truncated, any tool error, any tool result carrying `stale: true`; the reasons are stored and lead the email. Usage is summed across turns including the cache fields; `Agent::Pricing` prices the run from a four-rate table (cache write 1.25x, cache read 0.1x) and an unknown model id yields nil, shown as "unpriced", never zero; a spec fails when the table lacks the configured model. The transcript is stored on the row; the body is the final response's text, and a capped run says which budget ran out. Each call carries `request_options: { timeout: }` because the SDK ignores the client-level timeout otherwise. Prompts live in `app/models/agent/prompts/*.md.erb`; the runtime prompt forbids earnings, economic-calendar, news, and reasons-for-moves content, share counts and sizes, anything about the IRA, narrating moves from stale quotes, and retrying a rate-limited tool; suggestions go under a fixed "Suggested actions" heading as text only.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:120:**Briefs as email.** `Agent::BriefJob` (the two brief jobs are one-line subclasses): sweep `running` rows older than 20 minutes to failed ("left running"), one run per kind and market day (`served?` plus a partial unique index that lets a failed run be retried), a `skipped` row on a closed day, run whenever the calendar row says trading regardless of source (a fallback row is a degraded reason, "calendar unverified", not a skipped brief, so the token line still ships daily), wait up to 90 seconds for live feed or memory-pull runs so a 07:03 brief does not read positions mid-upsert or memory files mid-pull, then run, save, and deliver; whatever raises inside the run, the job finishes the row failed with the reason and delivers before re-raising. The email goes out whatever happened: `Brief` (app/models/brief.rb) frames the model's text with the token line, the degraded reasons, per-feed as-of stamps, the fixed sentence "Earnings and economic calendar: not available in Phase 1" on the morning brief, the end-of-day sections from the database (fills, journal rows touched, missing post-mortems with links, the day's snapshot or "not yet written; equity as of HH:MM"), template-generated links only, and a footer with turns, calls, tokens, cost, and the stop reason; a failed run says "The brief is unavailable: <error>". The model's text is rendered as plain text and, in the HTML part, escaped before `simple_format`, so a planted link or tag never renders. Subjects carry a `DEGRADED`, `CAPPED`, or `FAILED` prefix and no dollar figures. Recipients are every user (both seeded users get every brief, as with the token nag). `emailed_at` is stamped after delivery; `bin/rails agent:resend[ID]` re-sends a stored run without another API call, and `agent:brief[kind]` runs one now. `MEMORY_REPO_PATH` is read into `config.x.memory.repo_path`; `Memory::Repo` reads the six known files only, 32 KB per file and 128 KB total, scrubbed to UTF-8, snapshotted once per run. `ANTHROPIC_ADAPTER=fake` (the default outside production) swaps in `Agent::FakeAnthropic`, a scripted stand-in that returns canned `Anthropic::Models::Message` objects.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:124:## 4. Journal builder (zero-to-zero, trading-enabled accounts only; revised after the step 6 counselors review)
docs/phase-1-plan.md:128:**Bootstrap** (`Journal::BootstrapJob`, after every complete positions sync). Every open position in a trading-enabled account has one open trade. Its synthetic `entry` leg is a **reconciling plug**: quantity = broker quantity − net quantity of the linked fill legs, priced at the broker average price, recomputed after every bootstrap and link run and deleted when it reaches zero. A trade whose plug is non-zero is `bootstrapped: true, needs_review: true, review_reason: bootstrapped`, with `opened_at` nil. Positions with zero quantity or no average price are skipped. After a complete positions sync, an open trade whose instrument has no position and no unjournaled fills is flagged `review_reason: position_missing`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:131:- Buy fill, no open trade: open one. If `activity.order.order_proposal` resolves, copy setup, thesis, planned stop, and target; else `needs_review` with `review_reason: missing_setup`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:132:- Sell fill, no open trade: open a bootstrapped trade whose plug covers the pre-sale holding (position quantity + sold quantity when the position exists, else the sold quantity with `review_reason: bootstrapped`), then apply the exit.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:135:- Out-of-order arrival: when a newly linked activity precedes the latest leg on that instrument, the instrument's fills are replayed from scratch. Same-day fills with date-only timestamps are linked but flagged `review_reason: ordering_ambiguous`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:138:- Instrument-bearing `transfer` with an open trade (forward split, stock dividend, ACAT delivery): `adjustment` leg with ratio derived as (running + delivered) / running; quantity × ratio, prices ÷ ratio, `initial_risk` unchanged. Ratios that are not clean are flagged `review_reason: corporate_action`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:139:- `corporate_action` with two securities (CUSIP succession): both securities are read from the activity's `securities`; set `predecessor_instrument_id` on the new instrument and move the open trade to it with an adjustment leg. An unreviewed bootstrapped trade already on the new instrument is absorbed by the moved trade. Unmatched halves fall back to exit/entry with `review_reason: corporate_action`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:144:**R math.** `initial_quantity` = every entry fill sharing the first entry's `order_id` (fallback: all entries before the first exit), so a partial fill does not understate risk. `initial_risk` = `initial_quantity` × (average initial entry price − `planned_stop`), fixed once the stop is known; at or below zero it is nil and so is R. `realized_r` = `realized_pnl` / `initial_risk`. `total_risk` = sum over entry legs of quantity × (price − stop at that time), stored for the journal browser, never used as the R denominator. A bootstrapped trade closed before review takes setup and thesis only; its R stays nil.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:146:**Review path.** `review_reason` enum (missing_setup, missing_stop, bootstrapped, ordering_ambiguous, corporate_action, position_missing) drives the Monarch-style queue with Skip / Not a trade / Save. Save takes setup, planned stop, and thesis, clears `needs_review`, computes `initial_risk`, and audits `trade_reviewed`. Not a trade sets `excluded_from_stats`. The post-mortem quick entry (one line plus followed/improvised) is separate and available on any closed trade.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:148:**Setup stats** (`Journal::RecomputeSetupStatsJob`, after a trade closes, is reviewed, or is excluded): over closed trades with a positive `initial_risk`, not `needs_review`, not `excluded_from_stats`, and not bootstrapped-without-stop-at-entry: win rate (R > 0), average R, expectancy (mean R), sample size. Trailing-20 trend is deferred to the edge-review screen in Phase 2 and the plan says so.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:157:- Partially protected: remaining stop quantity below the position quantity. Shown as such, counted as unprotected in the portfolio total.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:158:- Oversized: remaining stop quantity above the position quantity. Schwab will reject the whole order at activation in a cash account, so this is flagged unprotected with its own reason (PRD §5.4.2 hard-alert case).
docs/phase-1-plan.md:160:- No stop, or a stop no longer working: unprotected.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:161:- Portfolio open risk sums protected positions only, and the dashboard and `get_account_health` state how many positions are excluded and why.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:165:## 6. Snapshots (per account, chain-linked; revised after the step 6 counselors review)
docs/phase-1-plan.md:171:- `open_risk_amount`, `open_risk_ratio`, `unprotected_count` from §5 at snapshot time.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:174:Dashboard day change is flow-adjusted (equity − flows − prior snapshot equity) and reads "no prior snapshot" on a gap day. The EOD fills recap reads activities journaled today; the missing-post-mortem list excludes `needs_review` and `excluded_from_stats` trades.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:178:## 7. UI (Hotwire, mobile-responsive, no JS routers, no hover-dependent modals; revised after the step 7 counselors review)
docs/phase-1-plan.md:182:**Model prerequisites built in this step.** `SchwabToken.status` (missing, revoked, expired, expiring, healthy; the Monday/Tuesday missed-Sunday nag stays in the health job) extracted from the health job and used by the banner, the system page, the mailer, and later `get_account_health`; `Account#sync_interval(feed)` and `Account#last_sync(feed)` extracted from the tick so views and scheduler cannot disagree; `trades.review_deferred_at` so Skip is durable ("later, not never": queue ordered by priority, then deferred-at nulls first, then oldest); `Position#distance_to_stop` guarded on a stop price rather than full protection so a partially covered stop still shows its distance; CASH_EQUIVALENT positions skipped by the positions sync so the sweep fund is neither a position nor a trade; `trading_enabled` requires `taxable`; an `account_configured` audit kind and an immediate sync enqueue when an account is enabled; setups creatable by name from the review form.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:186:| Dashboard | `/` | Banner by state: not connected (connect CTA); revoked (re-auth, with the refresh error); expired (re-auth, "sync paused since" from the first skipped run); expiring (re-auth, "Sunday's email will remind you" when covered); halted ("Halted by John, Mon 11:14a: reason. Clear it on the System page", no fake rule copy, re-auth link still shown if sync is also down); sync failed with a usable token (one-line status under the header, not a banner); needs setup (link to the accounts section). Equity with flow-adjusted change since the prior snapshot by date ("since Fri close" on a Monday, "first snapshot after today's close" before one exists); settled and unsettled cash ("unavailable", never zero, when both readings are nil); open risk labelled as known protected risk plus "N excluded: partial / oversized / awaiting / trailing / no stop"; positions as a list of rows sorted unprotected, awaiting, and trailing first then ascending distance, each with symbol, size, distance to stop as the primary number, the protection state inline, unrealized P&L (market value minus cost basis) second, and the older of the positions and orders as-of stamps; "N trades need review" callout; "Proposals: Phase 2" without a link; empty states for not connected, waiting for the first sync, and no open positions. |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:187:| Trade review | `/trades/:id/review` | Setup (pick or create by name), planned stop (validated below average entry with an explanatory error; "without a stop, R stays blank"), thesis; Save / Not a setup trade / Skip; "N more to review" |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:188:| Trade detail / post-mortem | `/trades`, `/trades/:id` | List with needs-review and missing-post-mortem filters (the EOD email deep-links there); detail with legs, planned versus actual stop (working stop for open trades, closing price when stopped out), R; the Flow 4 quick entry: required one line plus followed or improvised |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:189:| System | `/system` | Token status and age against 7 days with next Sunday 18:00 marked and a loud line when the token dies before it; last success and latest status per feed per account, `gap_from` when set, pause reason and since; failed sync runs plus Solid Queue failed executions in 7 days; shadow mode as a read-only indicator; API spend rendered as "0 runs, briefs start in step 9"; memory repo "never"; accounts table showing each account's equity and top symbols with an inline form for nickname, type, and enabled. Halt: set requires a reason and audits `manual_halt_set`; clear requires typed confirmation checked server-side and audits `manual_halt_cleared`. One word everywhere: Halt. |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:203:- **RSpec**, in the kickoff's priority order: token lifecycle with `travel_to` (25-minute refresh, 7-day expiry unaffected by refreshes, pause and catch-up, Mon/Tue escalation rule); sync jobs with fixture payloads (positions incl. removal, orders incl. cancel/replace and working stops, transactions incl. cash dividend, split, return of capital, CUSIP succession, fee items); journal linking (scale-in/out, orphan fill, sell-first legacy holding, bootstrap, ticker change on same CUSIP, R math); snapshot math (flows, late-landing deposit rebuild); MCP tool contracts (auth, each tool's schema and output, permission metadata excludes non-scheduled tools); scheduled runtime with a stubbed Messages API (turn cap, degraded mode).
docs/phase-1-plan.md:205:- **`Schwab::FakeClient`** implements the same interface as `Schwab::Client`, returns canned payloads, selected by `config.x.schwab.adapter`. Used by dev seeds and Playwright.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:206:- **Playwright** (`e2e/`, `@playwright/test` via npm, the only Node dependency): a scenarios route drawn only under `Rails.env.test?` and guarded again in the controller with `Schwab.fake?`, which resets the fake client, seeds with the factories (never by driving jobs), and signs in a seeded user by setting the session cookie because there is no inbox to read a magic link from. Times are relative: fresh is now, stale is three hours ago, expiring is 22 hours out, expired is two days ago. Scenarios: healthy, expiring, expired, halted, not connected, needs setup, one unprotected position, a failed sync with a usable token, the review queue with Skip persisting across reload, the post-mortem save, and re-auth success and failure (the seeded hash must match the fake's). The MCP endpoint is covered by request specs, not Playwright. The Playwright server runs with the test queue adapter.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:207:- **`bin/ci`**: Rails 8.1 `ActiveSupport::ContinuousIntegration` with steps in `config/ci.rb`, the pattern borrowed from Patchvault. Kickoff order: rubocop → rspec → brakeman (strict, warnings fail) → `bin/importmap audit` → `bundle exec bundle-audit check --update` → Playwright (`bin/playwright`, which boots a test-env server with the FakeClient, runs `npx playwright test`, and tears down). Fails on the first red step.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:211:## 9. Deploy (revised after the step 10 counselors review)
docs/phase-1-plan.md:214:- `Procfile`: `web: bin/rails server`, `worker: bin/jobs`, `release: bin/rails db:prepare` (dokku's release mechanism is the Procfile line; `app.json` carries the `formation` of web=1 worker=1 and a startup healthcheck on `/up`, which is excluded from host authorization). One Postgres database: Solid Queue, Solid Cache, and Solid Cable tables live in the primary schema (`InstallSolidTables`), so `db:prepare` on `DATABASE_URL` is the whole release. `db:prepare` seeds a fresh database, so `db/seeds.rb` creates the two users everywhere and the development desk only under `Rails.env.development? && Schwab.fake? && Agent.fake?`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:217:- Memory repo: the host owns the clone and the pull (PRD §5.6, "the VPS pulls the repo"); the container has no SSH client, no key, and `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`, so an in-container pull of a private remote was never going to work. `Memory::CheckRepoJob` records every half hour what the mount holds (succeeded with the file count, failed when the mount is missing or empty, nothing when no path is configured); an empty mount is a degraded reason on the brief, never a crash. `Memory::Repo#pull!` remains for development (`bin/rails memory:pull`).
docs/phase-1-plan.md:218:- Deploy restarts: a killed worker leaves `running` rows; `SyncRun.sweep_stale!` (10 minutes, run by the tick and the digest) and `AgentRun.sweep_stale!` (20 minutes) turn them into failures the system page and the digest show, and `AgentRun.served?` ignores a stale running row so the retried brief job still briefs. Avoid deploys 06:55 to 07:20 and 16:25 to 16:50; recovery is `bin/rails agent:brief[kind]`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:226:1. Tooling: RSpec, rubocop config, brakeman, bundler-audit, `bin/ci` (without Playwright), authentication generator adapted to magic link, AR encryption keys, credentials layout, crest in the layout.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:231:6. Journal builder (bootstrap, link, review path) + setup stats + snapshots.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:232:7. Dashboard, system health, trade screens; Playwright added to `bin/ci`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:234:9. Scheduled runtime + mailers (briefs, nags, failure digest) + memory repo pull.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:235:10. Seeds for dev via FakeClient; `Procfile`, `app.json`, `bin/dokku-setup`, the production database stanza and credential check; phase-level DHH pass and counselors review; first deploy.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:245:**Phase-level review (2026-09-01 night, DHH pass and counselors) — fixed before the first deploy:** a cash flow with no `netAmount` is `other` (quarantined), a flow with no amount is an unpriced flow the snapshot math quarantines, never zero (the dashboard, both briefs, and `get_account_health` used to 500 on it); a stop-covered position with no last price is the protection state `unpriced` (excluded from every risk sum and named), and open risk sums each live stop's tranche at its own stop price, with any priceless live stop making the pair `trailing_unknown`; `Order.terminal` is an unscoped subquery, so chaining it after `.working` cannot read as "not replaced by a live one"; a snapshot rebuild blocks rather than discards on its concurrency key (nothing re-enqueues one); the daily snapshot needs both positions and orders synced since the close (its risk columns are written once); working-stop detection skips a truncated orders page; a re-auth must cover every trading-enabled account (a read-only account left unticked is audited as `re_auth_missing_accounts`); `Instrument.resolve` names a CUSIP-only reference through Schwab's instrument lookup before giving up; stale activities are a degraded reason on the brief; account labels carry no hash fragment; `SyncRun.recent_first` breaks ties on id; `SystemSettings#writes_allowed?` is the one gate Phase 2 asks; dead scopes and constants (`Position.unprotected`, `protected_by_stop`, `Schwab::LOOKBACK`, `Client::TRANSACTION_TYPES`, `Order#container?`, `MarketDay#closed_by?`, `SystemSettings#halted?`) removed; `Jobs::FailureDigestJob` is `FailureDigestJob`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:247:**From the claude-fable phase review (narrowed rerun after two timeouts), fixed:** a snapshot uses only a post-close balance (the intraday fallback would have stamped an 11:00 equity as a close on catch-up and moved the high-water mark); the end-of-day sections say unknown, not none, while the activities feed is stale, and the equity line says stale; catch-up runs activities inline before enqueuing positions so a positions sync landing first cannot plug every trade bought during the pause; the plug price is in the plug's pre-split units; `get_account_health` reports a feed failure by the dashboard's rule (unresolved only); the dashboard's day change is unknown when a flow is unpriced; stop assignment runs only on a complete orders run (a truncated page or an unmapped or unresolved order skips it; a stop Schwab no longer returns does not).
docs/phase-1-plan.md:249:**Delisted holdings (added after the first deploy, 2026-09-01; a §5.2 column the user approved):** `instruments.delisted_at`, set and cleared from the system page (`InstrumentsController#update`, audited as `instrument_delisted` / `instrument_relisted`) and cleared by the positions sync when Schwab prices the holding again (audited as the system). A delisted holding still syncs and stays in the journal; its protection state is `delisted`, which leaves the unprotected count and every risk sum, sorts last on the dashboard, shows as one line in the excluded summary, and is named in the scheduled prompt as never to quote or count.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:251:**Deferred from the phase-level review (do before Phase 2, each gets more expensive weekly):** rename `Dashboard` to `Desk` (five consumers, one of them a screen) and `Agent::Run` to `Agent::Conversation`; fold `SystemStatus` onto the desk read model (halted_by, pause-since, last-sync-per-feed, and the token line are each written twice); one timestamp formatter per audience (the two locale formats for humans, `Agent.serialize` for machines; delete `Brief#stamp` and `Agent::Context#stamp`) and one cost label; move `Playwright::Scenario` to `lib/`; route `Agent::Context`'s setup stats through the registry or a shared method; add `audited` metadata to `Agent::Tool` for write tools; decide the activities policy when Schwab rejects one assumed type every run (today the run fails and re-backfills the window); `risk_rules` global uniqueness needs `NULLS NOT DISTINCT`; one trading account per desk (a validation collides with the factories; a partial unique index when Phase 2 needs it); `Instrument.lookup_cusip` can hit a token refresh inside the journal transaction (narrow); `Sync::CatchUpJob#perform` and the Playwright scenario loader have no Ruby-level specs; `Setup#avg_r` and `#expectancy` carry one number; the `market_hours` feed value is never written.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:255:Maintained in `docs/verify-on-approval.md` (30 items as of the step 3 contract review). The original seed list:
docs/phase-1-plan.md:275:1. **PRD review with counselors** (`counselors run`, agents `codex-5.5-high` and `claude-fable`): the relevant PRD sections plus this plan's section for the step. Findings are folded into the plan before code.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:277:3. **RSpec green** and reviewed for coverage against the §8 priority list, not just passing.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:278:4. **DHH skill review pass** (`dhh-code-reviewer` agent) on the step's diff; fix what it flags.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:279:5. **Counselors review of the build** (same two agents) on the diff; fix or explicitly decline each finding in the commit message.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:282:Counselors runs are long (10 to 20 minutes) and run in the background while unrelated work continues. Whole-phase gates: the counselors PRD review before step 1 (done, revision 2 of this plan is the result), and a DHH pass plus counselors review over the full Phase 1 diff after step 10.
