docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:85:- **Edge review** screen: per-setup table (win rate, avg R, expectancy, sample size, trailing-20 trend). Setups with negative expectancy flagged. Action per setup: deactivate (confirm dialog stating the effect: agent stops proposing this setup). Reactivation same path.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:89:List of rules with current parameters → edit one → before save, an effect preview: "Max risk 1.0% → 1.5% changes max position size at current equity from $X to $Y." Confirm to save. Every change is versioned with a timestamp (guardrail evaluations reference the rule version they ran against).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:95:List: symbol, trigger note ("break above 52.10 on volume"), added date, current price vs trigger. Add/edit/remove. The agent reads triggers; a trigger being met surfaces in the morning brief, not as a push (v1).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:110:Push (deep-link only, no figures in the payload): new proposal, fill/cancel, halt tripped, unprotected position, token expiring. Email: morning brief, EOD summary, Sunday ritual, job-failure digests. Original list:
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:112:- Morning brief (07:00), EOD summary (16:30), Sunday ritual
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:113:- New proposal awaiting review
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:133:- **Status pills in rows** (Pending, Failed) → proposal states in the queue and `unprotected` on positions.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:134:- **Reimbursement approval modal** (document left, status timeline right, one cancel action) → the post-approval timeline state, with the thesis panel where the invoice preview sits.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:142:- **Copilot Money (web), supplemental.** Three cards worth lifting: "Transactions to review" with its reviewed-everything empty state (our proposal queue on the dashboard), the range-chip row (1W / 1M / 3M / YTD / 1Y / ALL) on the net-worth chart, and "Next two weeks" as a dated upcoming list (our earnings/econ events touching the book).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:154:- **"Market recap" summary card**: the morning brief rendered in-app, not only emailed.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:160:**Monarch** is not on Mobbin. Worth screenshotting directly for the board: its transactions "needs review" queue and the net worth / holdings views are the closest consumer analogues to our proposal queue and dashboard.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:172:**Review modal → orphan-fill and incomplete-journal review.** "Is this merchant recurring? There are 9 more to review": entity card with recent transactions, a few form fields, and three actions (Skip / Not recurring / Save as recurring). Ours: "Is this fill part of a setup? N more to review", recent fills for the instrument, setup dropdown and planned stop, actions Skip / Not a trade / Save. The orange top banner with "Review now" is the pending-review entry point; the nav badge count (Recurring 10) is the proposals count on the rail.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:174:**Positions list, from the Accounts screen.** Per row: logo, name, sub-line, inline warning ("Account disconnected") where relevant, a small horizontal bar, a mini sparkline, amount, and a freshness stamp ("4 hours ago"). Ours: symbol, position size, inline "unprotected" warning, distance-to-stop bar, price sparkline, unrealized P&L, synced-at stamp. Collapsible group headers with group-level change and total serve the allocation view (positions grouped by target class).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:180:**AI-origin marker.** Monarch marks AI-generated content with a sparkle glyph next to the title (Weekly Recap, Budget, Spending). Adopt it: every agent-authored element (thesis, brief, review suggestion) carries the glyph, so human vs agent origin is legible at a glance. Ties to the origin field on proposals.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:182:**Also worth keeping:** "Your Weekly Recap · date range" card as the in-app entry to the Sunday review; "this month vs last year" comparison line for equity vs prior period; Recurring's "in 1 day" countdown for upcoming earnings/econ events and "settles Tue".
